<title>MALAYSIA: KL palm oil seen extending falls on bearish soyoil.</title>
<headline>KL palm oil seen extending falls on bearish soyoil.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysian palm oil prices are expected to open about five to seven ringgit lower on Wednesday in tandem with the bearish trend in Chicago soyoil futures.</p>
<p>* Sept resistance pegged at 1,175 ringgit</p>
<p>* Sept support - 1,140 ringgit</p>
<p>* Sept closed on Tuesday at 1,162 ringgit</p>
<p>* Prices seen staying in the 1,140-1,175 range on a lack of buying factors and the continuous fall in Chicago soyoil prices.</p>
<p>* Players also cautious of taking huge positions due to the traditionally high production figures in mid-year</p>
<p>($1=2.5220 ringgit)</p>
<p>-- By K. Baranee Krishnaan (603-230-7509)</p>
